$list — split prompt text into a texts array

SUMMARY
  Reads all input prompt link files, splits each prompt on commas and
  newlines, and appends one texts[] entry per non-empty segment. Clears
  prompts[] so downstream steps use discrete text items (e.g. model names,
  tags, or list values).

SYNTAX
  $list

INPUT
  prompts[] — one or more prompt files to split.

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one link per split token.
  prompts[] — cleared.

BEHAVIOR
  Splitting uses regex [,\\n]+ after trim. Empty segments are skipped.
  Typical use: instruction body "default, crazy_desire" with $list turns
  into two texts used as model=@image_models for $image.

EXAMPLE
  @image_models: $list
  default, crazy_desire

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes.
